#### **Task Table**

| Name       | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location        | Number of Robots | Justification                                                                 |
|------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|------------------|------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| AT1        | Place food on inpatient room table using special manipulation skill  | AND      | Inpatient Room   | [1]              | Requires one robot with specialized manipulation capability.                   |
| AT2        | Indicate which meal corresponds to the inpatient                     | AND      | Inpatient Room   | [1]              | Robot must identify the correct meal for the patient.                          |
| AT3        | Track when and where each meal was retrieved                         | AND      | Inpatient Room   | [1]              | Robot must log retrieval details for accountability.                           |
| AT4        | Alert if a wrong meal is retrieved                                   | AND      | Inpatient Room   | [1]              | Robot must detect and notify errors in meal retrieval.                         |
| AT5        | Retrieve dirty dishes from inpatient room                            | AND      | Inpatient Room   | [1]              | Requires one robot to collect dishes (unassisted).                             |
| AT6        | Retrieve dishes with cooperation (two robots or human)               | AND      | Inpatient Room   | [2]              | Requires two robots or a human-robot team for assistance.                      |

---

### **Logical Relationships**

- **G1 -> G2, G3, G5 [AND]**  
  - **Justification**: The mission requires receiving the order (G2), delivering the food (G3), and collecting dishes (G5) in sequence to complete the task.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [FALLBACK(G3.1, G3.2)]**  
  - **Justification**: The system must first attempt to allow retrieval (G3.2). If that fails (e.g., due to uncertainty in G4), it falls back to placing the food on the table (G3.1).

- **G3.2 -> G4, AT2, AT3, AT4 [AND]**  
  - **Justification**: Retrieval requires checking feasibility (G4), indicating the meal (AT2), tracking retrieval (AT3), and alerting errors (AT4) in sequence.

- **G5 -> G5.1, G5.2 [FALLBACK(G5.1, G5.2)]**  
  - **Justification**: The system first attempts unassisted dish retrieval (G5.1). If that fails, it falls back to using cooperation (G5.2).

- **G5.2 -> AT6 [AND]**  
  - **Justification**: Dish retrieval with cooperation requires the task AT6 (cooperative retrieval).

- **G4 -> G2, G6 [AND]**  
  - **Justification**: Feasibility of retrieval depends on the delivery request (G2) and whether someone can open the door (G6).

